<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jeonju</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wansanju</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jeonju is the capital of North Jeolla province in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>. Known as Wansanju in the Unified Silla period, it became the capital of Later Baekje when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyeon-hwon">Gyeon Hwon</a> proclaimed himself king there in 900. As the ancestral seat of the Jeonju Yi clan, the royal family of Joseon, it holds a shrine with a portrait of King Taejo, and it is known for its traditional houses and cuisine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jeonju.jpg" alt="Jeonju" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jeonju_Hanok_Maeul_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
